# Found by the model test (seed 6092). The rebase of b1 onto main stops on a conflict in
# z1/f.txt; `rebase --abort` first went back to the stopped tip (main), whose tree has d/e.txt,
# and deleted the user's UNTRACKED d/e.txt on the way. Abort must go straight to the original
# head and leave untracked files alone.
write d/e.txt 1
add d
commit
branch root b2
branch root b1
write z1/f.txt 2
add z1/f.txt
commit
checkout root b1
write z1/f.txt 0
delete d/e.txt
add .
write d/e.txt 0
commit
rebase root main
